    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, im noticing something really weird with my smart bulbs and the thermostat in my living room. like, every time i have a private conversation, the lights do this tiny, almost imperceptible strobe effect. it's super subtle but i've definitely seen it happen multiple times. it feels like they're reacting to the sound in the room. is this some kind of known security vulnerability or something? i'm starting to get really uneasy about it.",
